      "id": "85385abb646d",
      "name": "daily-strategist-audit",
      "prompt": "You are a Claude/Gemini strategist auditing Otto \u2014 an autonomous Hermes agent running on Chidi's machine.\n\nTURN DISCIPLINE (read first \u2014 you have a bounded turn budget):\n- Step 1 below is ONE `terminal` call. Do not read the nine paths one at a time.\n- Use single-command reads only. Do NOT pipe file contents into an interpreter\n  (`| python3`, `| sh`, `| bash`): the tirith security gate blocks that as\n  `pipe_to_interpreter` (HIGH) and the turn is wasted with no output.\n- This host is macOS: use `date -v-1d +%Y-%m-%d` for yesterday. GNU `date -d yesterday`\n  is an illegal option here and returns nothing.\n- Follow-up reads are fine, but batch them the same way (chain with `;`).\n\n1. **Read the current state** \u2014 run exactly this as a single terminal command:\n\necho \"=== REFLECTION ===\"; cat ~/.hermes/logs/reflection/$(date -v-1d +%Y-%m-%d).md 2>/dev/null; echo \"=== CORPUS ===\"; wc -c ~/.hermes/logs/self-regression-corpus.json; echo \"=== REGRESSION REPORT ===\"; cat ~/.hermes/logs/regression-report.md 2>/dev/null; echo \"=== MAINTENANCE ===\"; ls -t ~/.hermes/logs/maintenance/ | head -10; echo \"=== ALERTS ===\"; tail -200 ~/.hermes/logs/alerts/watchdog.jsonl 2>/dev/null; echo \"=== TRENDS ===\"; ls -t ~/.hermes/logs/trends/ | head -10; echo \"=== POLICIES ===\"; ls ~/.hermes/policies/; echo \"=== MASTER SPEC ===\"; head -120 ~/.hermes/specs/otto-system/00-MASTER.md 2>/dev/null; echo \"=== CRON JOBS ===\"; cat ~/.hermes/cron/jobs.json\n\n   The nine sections map to: yesterday's self-reflection, the failure corpus, latest\n   regression coverage, gap-finding/near-miss reports, active watchdog alerts,\n   cross-session trend analysis, all current policies, the architecture doc, and all\n   active cron jobs with last-run status.\n\n2. **Analyze:**\n   - Is coverage trending up? Is the corpus growing?\n   - Are there any active alerts that need immediate attention?\n   - What's the trend analysis saying about recurring patterns?\n   - Are there any dormant scripts/files that are created but never run?\n   - Are the idle learning jobs actually executing (check last_run_at)?\n   - What patterns do you see in recent corrections?\n   - Are there any contradictions between policies?\n\n3. **Recommend:**\n   - 2-3 specific improvements for today\n   - Any structural changes needed (not more policies \u2014 structural)\n   - Any scripts that should be deprecated or merged\n   - Any cron jobs that need attention\n\n4. **Output format:**\n   ```\n   ## Otto Audit \u2014 YYYY-MM-DD\n\n   **Policy health:** X active, Y provisional, Z retired\n   **Regression coverage:** X% (corpus: N entries)\n   **Uncovered failures:** [list top 3]\n   **Active alerts:** [N from watchdog]\n\n   ### \ud83d\udd34 Issues\n   ### \ud83d\udfe1 Warnings\n   ### \ud83d\udfe2 Good\n   ### \ud83d\udca1 Improvement suggestions for today\n   ```\n\n   Write the full report to `~/.hermes/reports/strategist-audit-$(date +%Y-%m-%d).md`\n   EARLY \u2014 as soon as you have the findings, before composing the summary \u2014 then deliver\n   the summary here. Do not leave the write to the last turn.",
